<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.16.6: Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01159</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.16.6: Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bc1f90ee-aadc-462c-a8cc-ae4b0fe46ddf</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    Explain what it means for a sequence to be arithmetic or geometric.
  </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities </emphasis>that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    4.16.1: Interpreting Function Notation
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you mentally evaluated functions given a function in function notation.
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.16.2: What Is an Arithmetic Sequence?
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you learned what makes a sequence arithmetic.
    </item>
    <item>
      4.16.2: Self Check
    </item>
    <item>
      4.16.2: Additional Resources 
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.16.3: A Sequence Is a Type of Function
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you represented a sequence in a graph and discussed if it could be geometric or arithmetic.
    </item>
    <item>
      4.16.3: Self Check
    </item>
    <item>
      4.16.3: Additional Resources 
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.16.4: Identify and Generate Sequences
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you completed the same sequence with different terms to make it arithmetic, then geometric, and then neither.
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para>After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    4.16.5: Practice
  </item>
</list>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Checking In</title><exercise data-content-id="75e54e0b-b165-496a-98b8-25a5f4f52a92"><problem><para>
      <para>On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson? </para>
    </para></problem><solution><newline/><para>
      <para>Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
